EOF
```

This is a **source prediction; it was not executed**. It shows the local behavior, but the supplied contract does not say whether the two calls represent a duplicate delivery or two payments.

The appropriate next step is to establish the repeated-ID and delivery semantics. If IDs must identify payments uniquely and duplicate deliveries must be ignored, the handler needs a deduplication rule and an atomic way to persist the ID with the balance change. That change would risk dropping legitimate payments if repeated IDs are allowed to represent separate payments.

